:: ChildhoodInjury [childhood]
# A Painful Lesson

While playing near the edge of camp, you fall and cut your leg on a sharp stone. The pain is immediate and intense, bringing tears to your eyes. Blood trickles from the wound, frightening you even more than the pain.

Your cries bring adults running. Your mother reaches you first, quickly examining the injury.

"It's not too deep," she says reassuringly, though her face shows concern. "We must clean it to prevent bad spirits from entering the wound."

She calls for the shaman, who brings healing materials - clean water, herbs, and a poultice made from specific plants. The shaman cleans the wound carefully, chanting softly while applying the medicine.

"Be brave, little one," the shaman tells you. "This pain will teach you to be more careful, but it will pass."

The adults explain that injuries are part of life, but knowing how to treat them is essential knowledge for survival.

<<set $needs.health -= 10>>

